@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- MSIG Insurance (Vietnam) Company Limited, General Liability Insurance Policy
-- ("Revised General Liability Policy Form", the file dated 12 January 2015).
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every other module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../source/raw/msig-cgl.txt, the `pdftotext -layout` rendering of
-- msig-cgl.pdf (sha256 cb17d805...3814), retrieved 2026-10-06 from msig.com.vn.
-- The source is ENGLISH ONLY. A `src:N` comment quotes line N of the text file and is
-- generated by tools/vnsrc.py; nothing quoted here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is a bare NUMBER. The policy states no currency for the limits it leaves to the
-- schedule; this encoding reads every sum as Vietnamese dong (VND), the brief's
-- convention. The only figures the document prints are in US dollars and Singapore
-- dollars (src:28, 34, 942, 949); those are converted at rates the caller supplies
-- (NOTES.md, forks F4 and F5).
--
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to
-- the fact, or the declarations, the schedule or a claim file record it. Whether the
-- fact puts a claim inside or outside the cover is a rule, and lives in the module for
-- the clause that says so.

§ `Nouns for the MSIG general liability policy`

§§ `The coverage parts and the declarations`

-- src:12 says cover is afforded by the Coverage Parts the declarations identify. The
-- form prints two.
DECLARE `A coverage part` IS ONE OF
    `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part`
    `the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part`

-- Persons Insured (a)-(c) of both parts turn on how the declarations designate the
-- named insured (src:464-473, 645-654).
DECLARE `A designation of the named insured` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a partnership or joint venture`
    `an organization other than an individual, partnership or joint venture`

-- Limits of Liability (src:508-522, 669-683) refer to separate bodily injury and property
-- damage limits "stated in the schedule"; the Combined Single Limit Endorsement
-- (src:805-810) refers to one "each occurrence" sum and one "aggregate" sum. Which of the
-- two the schedule states is a fact about this policy (NOTES.md, fork F10).
DECLARE `The limits stated in the schedule` IS ONE OF
    `separate limits for bodily injury and property damage` HAS
        `bodily injury, each occurrence`   IS A NUMBER
        `bodily injury, aggregate`         IS A NUMBER
        `property damage, each occurrence` IS A NUMBER
        `property damage, aggregate`       IS A NUMBER
    `a combined single limit` HAS
        `each occurrence` IS A NUMBER
        `aggregate`       IS A NUMBER

-- The declarations and the schedule, as far as the document refers to them.
-- `the policy period ends`: the date stated, or, after a cancellation, the date
-- Condition 9 makes the end of the policy period (src:293-294).
-- `the retroactive date stated in the policy schedule`: src:754 leaves it to the schedule;
-- NOTHING where the schedule states none.
DECLARE `The policy as declared` HAS
    `coverage parts identified in the declarations`        IS A LIST OF `A coverage part`
    `the named insured is designated in the declarations as` IS A `A designation of the named insured`
    `the policy period begins`                              IS A DATE
    `the policy period ends`                                IS A DATE
    `the retroactive date stated in the policy schedule`    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the limits stated in the schedule`                     IS A `The limits stated in the schedule`

§§ `The claim`

-- Persons Insured (src:462-499, 643-660) and Condition 8 (src:281-285) name the people
-- who are insureds. The case says which of them the claim is made against, in the
-- words of those clauses; "another person or organization" is everyone else.
DECLARE `A person claimed against` IS ONE OF
    `the named insured`
    `the spouse of the named insured`
    `a partner or member of the named insured`
    `an executive officer, director or stockholder of the named insured`
    `a person who is not an employee of the named insured, or an organization, acting as real estate manager for the named insured`
    `an employee of the named insured`
    `a person other than an employee of the named insured, operating mobile equipment`
    `a person or organization legally responsible for the operation of mobile equipment`
    `the legal representative of the named insured, who has died`
    `the person having proper temporary custody of the property of the named insured, who has died`
    `another person or organization`

-- The definitions of "bodily injury" (src:59-60) and "property damage" (src:164-166)
-- name three kinds of harm. Anything else (a purely financial loss, say) is the fourth.
DECLARE `A kind of harm` IS ONE OF
    `bodily injury, sickness or disease sustained by a person`
    `physical injury to or destruction of tangible property`
    `loss of use of tangible property which has not been physically injured or destroyed`
    `harm of another kind`

-- A Claim Series Event (src:762-776): the dates its clauses turn on. Whether the claim
-- belongs to such a series is a finding (below); these dates are needed only if it does.
DECLARE `A claim series` HAS
    `the date the first loss of the series occurred`                                IS A DATE
    `the date the first claim of the series was made in writing against the insured` IS A DATE
    `the date the insured was first advised in writing of the first claim of the series` IS A DATE
    `the date written notice of the series was given to the Company or an authorized agent` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- One claim by one claimant against one insured (the Claims Made Basis Endorsement,
-- src:738-741, deems each claimant's claim made on that claimant's behalf alone, and
-- the definition of "insured", src:121-122, applies the insurance separately to each
-- insured). Dates are calendar dates.
-- * `the date the injury occurs`: when the bodily injury, or the physical injury to or
--   destruction of property, occurs (src:59, 164).
-- * `the date of the occurrence`: the accident that causes the harm; property damage of
--   the third kind (loss of use alone) is dated by it (src:166).
-- * `the occurrence` and `the general conditions of exposure`: labels the caller gives,
--   so that harms can be counted as one occurrence (src:542-544, 685-687, 812-814).
-- * `the date the claim was first made in writing against an insured`: NOTHING if no
--   claim has been made yet.
-- * the two notice-of-circumstances dates: Claims Made Basis Endorsement clause 4
--   (src:746-750); NOTHING where there was no such awareness or notice.
DECLARE `A claim against an insured` HAS
    `the person claimed against`                                       IS A `A person claimed against`
    `the harm`                                                         IS A `A kind of harm`
    `the date the injury occurs`                                       IS A DATE
    `the date of the occurrence`                                       IS A DATE
    `the occurrence`                                                   IS A STRING
    `the general conditions of exposure`                               IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the date the claim was first made in writing against an insured`  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date an insured first became aware of circumstances which may give rise to the claim` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date written notice of those circumstances was given to the Company` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the claim series`                                                 IS A MAYBE `A claim series`
    `the findings`                                                     IS A LIST OF `A finding`

§§ `What the record may find`

-- Each fact below is one a witness could testify to, worded as the clause that reads it
-- words it. A claim's record holds FINDINGS: that a fact is the case, or that it is not.
-- A fact the record does not mention is not assumed either way: a rule that needs it
-- refuses, naming it (msig-cgl-record.l4). The refusal table there is generated from
-- this list by script, so the two cannot drift.
--
-- "the vehicle" is the land vehicle the claim arises out of, if any; "the device" is the
-- hoisting device of the elevator limb; "the conveyance" is the automobile, aircraft or
-- watercraft concerned; "that contract or agreement" is the one under which the insured
-- assumed liability; "the damaged property" is the property the property damage is to.
DECLARE `A fact` IS ONE OF
    -- I. the insuring agreement (src:325-336, 563-575); "occurrence" (src:139-140)
    `the insured is legally obligated to pay the sums claimed as damages`
    `the harm results from an accident, including continuous or repeated exposure to conditions`
    `the harm was expected or intended from the standpoint of the insured`
    -- "policy territory" (src:142-157) and IV (src:549, 692)
    `the harm occurs within a nation or area described in the Policy`
    `the harm occurs in international waters or air space`
    `the harm occurs in the course of travel or transportation to or from another nation or area`
    `the damages arise out of a product sold for use or consumption within the territory described in the Policy`
    `a suit for the damages has been brought`
    `the original suit for the damages was brought in a court of competent jurisdiction within Vietnam`
    -- JURISDICTION (src:46-49)
    `the insured's liability for the damages is fixed by a judgement`
    `the judgement was delivered in the first instance by, or obtained from, a court of competent jurisdiction within Vietnam`
    `the judgement is an order of a Vietnamese court for the enforcement of a judgement made outside Vietnam`
    -- "products hazard" (src:159-162); "named insured products" (src:135-137)
    `the harm arises out of the named insured's products, or reliance upon a representation or warranty made at any time about them`
    `those products are a vending machine, or other property apart from a container, rented to or located for use of others but not sold`
    `the harm occurs away from premises owned by or rented to the named insured`
    `physical possession of those products had been relinquished to others when the harm occurred`
    -- "completed operations hazard" (src:74-100)
    `the harm arises out of operations, including materials, parts or equipment furnished with them, or reliance upon a representation or warranty made at any time about them`
    `all operations to be performed by or on behalf of the named insured under the contract had been completed when the harm occurred`
    `all operations to be performed by or on behalf of the named insured at the site had been completed when the harm occurred`
    `the portion of the work out of which the harm arises had been put to its intended use, when the harm occurred, by a person or organization other than another contractor or subcontractor engaged in performing operations for a principal as part of the same project`
    `the operations had been abandoned when the harm occurred`
    `the operations were otherwise complete when the harm occurred, though they might require further service or maintenance work, or correction, repair or replacement because of a defect or deficiency`
    `the harm arises out of operations in connection with the transportation of property`
    `the harm arises out of a condition in or on a vehicle created by its loading or unloading`
    `the harm arises out of the existence of tools, uninstalled equipment or abandoned or unused materials`
    `the classification stated in the Policy or in the Company's manual for the operations specifies including completed operations`
    -- "collapse hazard" (src:62-73)
    `the property damage is the collapse of or structural injury to a building or structure, or results at any time from such collapse or injury`
    `the collapse or structural injury is due to grading of land, excavating, borrowing, filling, back-filling, tunnelling, pile driving, cofferdam work or caisson work`
    `the collapse or structural injury is due to moving, shoring, underpinning, raising or demolition of a building or structure, or removal or rebuilding of its structural support`
    `the harm arises out of operations performed for the named insured by independent contractors`
    -- "explosion hazard" (src:109-113)
    `the property damage arises out of blasting or explosion`
    `the property damage arises out of the explosion of air or steam vessels, piping under pressure, prime movers, machinery or power transmitting equipment`
    -- "underground property damage hazard" (src:168-175)
    `the property damage is to wires, conduits, pipes, mains, sewers, tanks, tunnels, similar property or apparatus connected with them, beneath the surface of the ground or water, or results at any time from such damage`
    `that underground damage was caused by and occurred during the use of mechanical equipment for grading land, paving, excavating, drilling, borrowing, filling, back-filling or pile driving`
    -- contractual liability: exclusion (a) of both parts; "incidental contract" (src:115-118)
    `the insured assumed liability for the harm under a contract or agreement`
    `that contract or agreement is in writing`
    `that contract or agreement is a lease of premises`
    `that contract or agreement is an easement agreement`
    `that easement agreement is in connection with construction or demolition operations on or adjacent to a railroad`
    `that contract or agreement is an undertaking to indemnify a municipality required by municipal ordinance`
    `that undertaking is in connection with work for the municipality`
    `that contract or agreement is a sidetrack agreement`
    `that contract or agreement is an elevator maintenance agreement`
    `the liability is under a warranty of fitness or quality of the named insured's products`
    `the liability is under a warranty that work performed by or on behalf of the named insured will be done in a workmanlike manner`
    -- "automobile" (src:56-57) and "mobile equipment" (src:124-131)
    `the vehicle is a land motor vehicle, trailer or semi-trailer designed for travel on public roads`
    `the vehicle is a land vehicle`
    `the vehicle is not subject to motor vehicle registration`
    `the vehicle is maintained for use exclusively on premises owned by or rented to the named insured, including the ways immediately adjoining`
    `the vehicle is designed for use principally off public roads`
    `the vehicle is designed or maintained for the sole purpose of affording mobility to equipment of a type the definition of mobile equipment lists, forming an integral part of it or permanently attached to it`
    -- CGL exclusions (b)-(e) (src:346-371)
    `the harm arises out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of the vehicle`
    `the harm arises out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of an aircraft`
    `the harm arises out of the ownership, maintenance, operation, use, loading or unloading of a watercraft`
    `the conveyance is owned by an insured`
    `the conveyance is operated by an insured`
    `the conveyance is rented or loaned to an insured`
    `the conveyance is operated by a person in the course of employment by an insured`
    `the harm arises out of the parking of the vehicle on premises owned by, rented to or controlled by the named insured, or the ways immediately adjoining`
    `the vehicle was being used in a prearranged or organized racing, speed or demolition contest, in a stunting activity, or in practice or preparation for such a contest or activity`
    `the harm arises out of the operation or use of a snowmobile or a trailer designed for use with one`
    `the harm arises out of and in the course of the transportation of the vehicle by an automobile owned or operated by, or rented or loaned to, an insured`
    `the watercraft was ashore on premises owned by, rented to or controlled by the named insured`
    -- CGL exclusion (f), P&CO exclusion (i): pollution (src:373-376, 630-637)
    `the harm arises out of the discharge, dispersal, release or escape of smoke, vapors, soot, fumes, acids, alkalis, toxic chemicals, liquids or gases, waste materials or other irritants, contaminants or pollutants into or upon land, the atmosphere or a water course or body of water`
    `that discharge, dispersal, release or escape was sudden and accidental`
    -- CGL exclusion (g): war (src:378-383)
    `the harm is due to war, whether or not declared, civil war, insurrection, rebellion or revolution, or an act or condition incident to any of them`
    -- CGL exclusion (h), P&CO exclusion (b): alcoholic beverages (src:385-403, 585-601)
    `the insured may be held liable as a person or organization engaged in the business of manufacturing, distributing, selling or serving alcoholic beverages`
    `the insured may be held liable, not being so engaged, as an owner or lessor of premises used for such purposes`
    `the insured's indemnitee may be held liable as a person or organization engaged in the business of manufacturing, distributing, selling or serving alcoholic beverages`
    `the insured's indemnitee may be held liable, not being so engaged, as an owner or lessor of premises used for such purposes`
    `the liability is imposed by, or because of the violation of, a statute, ordinance or regulation pertaining to the sale, gift, distribution or use of an alcoholic beverage`
    `the liability is imposed by reason of selling, serving or giving an alcoholic beverage to a minor or to a person under the influence of alcohol, or which causes or contributes to the intoxication of a person`
    -- CGL exclusions (i)-(j), P&CO (c)-(d) (src:405-410, 603-607)
    `the claim is for an obligation for which the insured or a carrier as its insurer may be held liable under a workmen's compensation, unemployment compensation or disability benefits law, or a similar law`
    `the bodily injury is to an employee of the insured, arising out of and in the course of employment by the insured`
    -- CGL exclusion (k) (src:412-423); "elevator" (src:102-107)
    `the damaged property is owned or occupied by, or rented to, the insured`
    `the damaged property is used by the insured`
    `the damaged property is in the care, custody or control of the insured, or the insured is for any purpose exercising physical control over it`
    `the property damage arises out of the use of the device at premises owned by, rented to or controlled by the named insured`
    `the damaged property is the device`
    `the device is a hoisting or lowering device to connect floors or landings`
    `the device is an automobile servicing hoist`
    `the device is a hoist without a platform outside a building, without mechanical power or not attached to building walls`
    `the device is a hod or material hoist used in alteration, construction or demolition operations`
    `the device is an inclined conveyor used exclusively for carrying property`
    `the device is a dumbwaiter used exclusively for carrying property and having a compartment height not exceeding four feet`
    -- CGL exclusion (l) (src:425)
    `the damaged property is premises alienated by the named insured`
    `the property damage arises out of those premises or any part of them`
    -- CGL exclusion (m), P&CO exclusion (e) (src:427-436, 609-618)
    `the loss of use results from a delay in or lack of performance by or on behalf of the named insured of a contract or agreement`
    `the loss of use results from the failure of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured to meet the level of performance, quality, fitness or durability warranted or represented by the named insured`
    `the loss of use results from sudden and accidental physical injury to or destruction of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured, after they had been put to use by a person or organization other than an insured`
    -- CGL exclusions (n)-(p), P&CO (f)-(h) (src:438-446, 620-628)
    `the damaged property is the named insured's products`
    `the property damage arises out of those products or any part of them`
    `the damaged property is work performed by or on behalf of the named insured`
    `the property damage arises out of that work or any portion of it, or out of materials, parts or equipment furnished in connection with it`
    `the damages are claimed for the withdrawal, inspection, repair, replacement or loss of use of the named insured's products or work completed by or for the named insured, or of property of which they form a part`
    `those products, that work or that property were withdrawn from the market or from use because of a known or suspected defect or deficiency in them`
    -- CGL exclusion (q) (src:448-457)
    `the operations are identified in the Policy by a classification code number which includes the symbol x`
    `the operations are identified in the Policy by a classification code number which includes the symbol c`
    `the operations are identified in the Policy by a classification code number which includes the symbol u`
    -- II. Persons Insured (src:462-499, 643-660); Condition 8 (src:281-285)
    `the claim concerns the conduct of a business of which the named insured is the sole proprietor`
    `the liability is that of the partner or member as such`
    `the executive officer, director or stockholder was acting within the scope of their duties as such`
    `the harm arises out of the operation, for the purpose of locomotion upon a public highway, of mobile equipment registered under a motor vehicle registration law`
    `the employee was operating the mobile equipment in the course of employment`
    `the mobile equipment is registered in the name of the named insured`
    `the person was operating the mobile equipment with the permission of the named insured`
    `other valid and collectible insurance is available, on a primary or excess basis, to the person or organization claimed against`
    `the bodily injury is to a fellow employee of the operator, injured in the course of employment`
    `the damaged property is owned by, rented to, in charge of or occupied by the named insured or the employer of the operator`
    `the harm arises out of the conduct of a partnership or joint venture of which the insured is a partner or member and which is not designated in the Policy as a named insured`
    `the legal representative is acting within the scope of their duties as such`
    `the claim is with respect to the property of the named insured`
    `a legal representative of the named insured has been appointed and qualified`
    -- Claims Made Basis Endorsement (src:731-752) and Claim Series Clause (src:765)
    `immediate notice of the harm has been given in accordance with the Conditions`
    `at the effective date of the policy an insured knew that the harm might be expected to be the basis of a claim or suit`
    `at the effective date of the policy an insured could reasonably have foreseen that the harm might be expected to be the basis of a claim or suit`
    `the harm has been, or is alleged to have been, caused to any extent or degree, directly or indirectly, before the Retroactive Date`
    `the claim arises out of the named insured's products to which the notified circumstances relate`
    `the claim is one of a series of two or more claims arising from one specific common cause attributable to one design, specification or formula in products or services supplied by one insured`
    -- Business Risk Exclusion (src:720-724)
    `the harm results from the failure of the named insured's products or work performed by or on behalf of the named insured to perform the function or to serve the purpose intended by the named insured`
    `that failure is due to a mistake or deficiency in a design, formula, plan, specifications, advertising material or printed instructions prepared or developed by an insured`
    `the harm results from the active malfunctioning of those products or that work`
    -- Asbestos Exclusion (src:785-791)
    `the claim or loss is based upon, arises out of, directly or indirectly results from, is in consequence of, or in any way involves asbestos`
    `the claim or loss in any way involves actual or alleged asbestos related injury or damage involving the use, presence, existence, detection, removal, elimination or avoidance of asbestos, or exposure or potential exposure to asbestos`
    -- Cyber Liability Exclusion (src:819-821)
    `the claim or loss arises out of activities or business conducted or transacted via the Internet, an Intranet or an Extranet`
    `the claim or loss arises out of activities or business conducted or transacted via the insured's own website, Internet site or web address`
    `the claim or loss arises out of activities or business conducted or transacted via the transmission of electronic mail or documents by electronic means`
    -- Date Recognition Exception (src:826-843)
    `the claim arises directly or indirectly from, or consists of, the failure or inability of an electronic circuit, microchip, computer, software, telecommunication equipment or similar device, or media or systems used with one, whether the insured's property or not, to achieve a purpose or effect intended by the use of a number, symbol or word to denote a date`
    `that failure or inability is a result of recognising, using or adopting a date, day of the week or period of time otherwise than as, or other than, the true or correct one`
    `that failure or inability is a result of the operation of a command or logic programmed or incorporated into such a device, media or system`
    -- Electromagnetic Fields Exclusion (src:848-849)
    `the loss or liability arises out of, or is contributed to directly or indirectly by, exposure to magnetic, electric or electromagnetic fields or radiation, however caused or generated`
    -- Institute Radioactive Contamination ... Exclusion Clause (src:860-877)
    `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from ionising radiations from or contamination by radioactivity from nuclear fuel, nuclear waste or the combustion of nuclear fuel`
    `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from the radioactive, toxic, explosive or other hazardous or contaminating properties of a nuclear installation, reactor or other nuclear assembly or nuclear component`
    `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from a weapon or device employing atomic or nuclear fission or fusion or other like reaction or radioactive force or matter`
    `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from the radioactive, toxic, explosive or other hazardous or contaminating properties of radioactive matter`
    `that radioactive matter is radioactive isotopes, other than nuclear fuel, being prepared, carried, stored or used for commercial, agricultural, medical, scientific or other similar peaceful purposes`
    `the loss, damage, liability or expense is directly or indirectly caused by, contributed to by or arises from a chemical, biological, bio-chemical or electromagnetic weapon`
    -- Professional Liability Exclusion (src:882-883)
    `the liability arises out of breach of professional duty, or wrongful or inadequate advice given separately for a fee`
    -- Sanction Limitation and Exclusion Clause (src:894-897)
    `providing the cover or paying the claim would expose the Company to a sanction, prohibition or restriction under United Nations resolutions or the trade or economic sanctions, laws or regulations of the European Union, the United Kingdom or the United States of America`
    -- Sistership Exclusion Clause (src:904-912)
    `the harm arises from the same cause as an earlier bodily injury or property damage`
    `after that earlier injury or damage the named insured failed to take the preventive measures the Sistership Exclusion Clause requires`
    `the named insured had a justifiable reason for that failure`
    -- War and Terrorism Exclusion (src:954-977)
    `the loss is directly or indirectly caused by, results from or is in connection with war, invasion, acts of foreign enemies, hostilities or warlike operations, civil war, rebellion, revolution, insurrection, civil commotion assuming the proportions of or amounting to an uprising, or military or usurped power`
    `the loss is directly or indirectly caused by, results from or is in connection with an act of terrorism`
    `the loss is directly or indirectly caused by, results from or is in connection with an action taken in controlling, preventing, suppressing or in any way relating to war or terrorism`
    `the Company alleges that by reason of the War and Terrorism Exclusion the loss is not covered`
    `the insured has proved that the loss is not excluded by the War and Terrorism Exclusion`
    -- Limits of Liability, CGL III, Coverage B aggregate (src:524-533)
    `the property damage arises out of premises or operations rated on a remuneration basis, or contractor's equipment rated on a receipts basis`
    `the property damage arises out of and occurs in the course of operations performed for the named insured by independent contractors and general supervision thereof by the named insured`
    `the property damage arises out of maintenance or repairs at premises owned by or rented to the named insured, or structural alterations there which do not involve changing the size of or moving buildings or other structures`
    -- Condition 4, Action Against Company (src:231-234)
    `there has been full compliance with all of the terms of the Policy`
    `the insured's obligation to pay has been finally determined by judgement against the insured after actual trial`
    `the insured's obligation to pay has been finally determined by written agreement of the insured, the claimant and the Company`

-- A finding about one fact. The record is a list of findings; the first finding about a
-- fact is the one read, so a scenario can be written as one finding put in front of a
-- baseline.
DECLARE `A finding` IS ONE OF
    `it is the case that`     HAS `the fact` IS A `A fact`
    `it is not the case that` HAS `the fact` IS A `A fact`

§§ `The sums for one occurrence`

-- The amounts the Supplementary Payments clause (src:18-34) and the Ultimate Net Loss
-- Clause (src:926-949) count, for all claims arising out of one occurrence, in dong.
-- * `the cost of each bail bond` and `the actual loss of earnings for each day` are lists,
--   one entry per bond and per day, because each is capped separately (src:28, 34,
--   942, 949).
-- * `fines, penalties, punitive, exemplary, treble or multiplied damages`: the part of
--   the award the Punitive Damages Exclusion (src:888-889) takes out.
-- * `sums the insured voluntarily paid, assumed or incurred, other than for first aid`:
--   Condition 3(c) leaves them at the insured's own cost (src:226-227).
-- * `expenses of withdrawal, inspection, repair or replacement, or of other preventive
--   measures`: the Sistership Exclusion Clause paragraph 3 does not indemnify them
--   (src:914-916).
DECLARE `The sums for one occurrence` HAS
    `damages because of bodily injury`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `damages because of property damage`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `fines, penalties, punitive, exemplary, treble or multiplied damages`       IS A NUMBER
    `expenses incurred by the Company`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `costs taxed against the insured in a suit defended by the Company`        IS A NUMBER
    `interest accruing after entry of judgement and before the Company pays, tenders or deposits its part` IS A NUMBER
    `premiums on appeal bonds`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `premiums on bonds to release attachments, for an amount not in excess of the applicable limit` IS A NUMBER
    `the cost of each bail bond`                                               IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `expenses incurred by the insured for first aid to others at the time of the accident` IS A NUMBER
    `reasonable expenses incurred by the insured at the Company's request, other than loss of earnings` IS A NUMBER
    `the actual loss of earnings for each day`                                 IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `sums the insured voluntarily paid, assumed or incurred, other than for first aid` IS A NUMBER
    `expenses of withdrawal, inspection, repair or replacement, or of other preventive measures` IS A NUMBER

-- The document prints its only figures in foreign currency and gives no rule for
-- converting them (NOTES.md, fork F5). The caller supplies the rate used.
DECLARE `Rates of exchange into dong` HAS
    `dong per United States dollar` IS A NUMBER
    `dong per Singapore dollar`     IS A NUMBER

-- What has already been paid out of each aggregate limit before this occurrence.
-- `under the property damage aggregate that applies`: the CGL Coverage B aggregate
-- applies separately to each numbered category, and to each project away from the named
-- insured's premises (src:538-540); the caller gives the figure for the category and
-- project this occurrence falls in.
DECLARE `Amounts already paid under the aggregate limits` HAS
    `under the combined aggregate`                     IS A NUMBER
    `under the bodily injury aggregate`                IS A NUMBER
    `under the property damage aggregate that applies` IS A NUMBER

§§ `The answers the document can give`

-- Why a claim is not covered: one member per clause that can defeat a claim, named for
-- the clause. Used by msig-cgl-answer.l4.
DECLARE `A reason there is no cover` IS ONE OF
    `COVERAGE: the coverage part is not identified in the declarations`
    `PERSONS INSURED: the person claimed against is not an insured`
    `PERSONS INSURED: the conduct of a partnership or joint venture not designated as a named insured`
    `I: the insured is not legally obligated to pay the damages`
    `I: the harm is neither bodily injury nor property damage as defined`
    `I: the harm did not occur during the policy period`
    `I: the harm was not caused by an occurrence`
    `I: the harm is not within the completed operations hazard or the products hazard`
    `IV: the harm did not occur within the policy territory`
    `JURISDICTION: the judgement was not delivered in the first instance by a court in Vietnam`
    `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: the claim was not made during the policy period`
    `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: the harm was not sustained after the Retroactive Date`
    `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: immediate notice was not given`
    `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: the harm was known and foreseeable at the effective date`
    `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 3: the harm was caused before the Retroactive Date`
    `CLAIM SERIES 4: the claim was made more than 120 months after the first claim`
    `CGL exclusion (a): liability assumed under a contract`
    `CGL exclusion (b): automobiles and aircraft`
    `CGL exclusion (c): mobile equipment in a contest, and snowmobiles`
    `CGL exclusion (d): mobile equipment carried by an insured's automobile`
    `CGL exclusion (e): watercraft`
    `CGL exclusion (f): pollution`
    `CGL exclusion (g): war, for incidental contracts`
    `CGL exclusion (h): alcoholic beverages`
    `CGL exclusion (i): workmen's compensation and similar laws`
    `CGL exclusion (j): injury to the insured's employees`
    `CGL exclusion (k): property owned, used or controlled by the insured`
    `CGL exclusion (l): premises alienated by the named insured`
    `CGL exclusion (m): loss of use from delay or failure to perform`
    `CGL exclusion (n): damage to the named insured's products`
    `CGL exclusion (o): damage to the named insured's work`
    `CGL exclusion (p): withdrawal of products or work`
    `CGL exclusion (q): explosion, collapse and underground hazards`
    `P&CO exclusion (a): liability assumed under a contract`
    `P&CO exclusion (b): alcoholic beverages`
    `P&CO exclusion (c): workmen's compensation and similar laws`
    `P&CO exclusion (d): injury to the insured's employees`
    `P&CO exclusion (e): loss of use from delay or failure to perform`
    `P&CO exclusion (f): damage to the named insured's products`
    `P&CO exclusion (g): damage to the named insured's work`
    `P&CO exclusion (h): withdrawal of products or work`
    `P&CO exclusion (i): pollution`
    `COMPLETED OPERATIONS HAZARD AND PRODUCTS HAZARD EXCLUSION CLAUSE`
    `BUSINESS RISK EXCLUSION`
    `ASBESTOS EXCLUSION`
    `CYBER LIABILITY EXCLUSION`
    `DATE RECOGNITION EXCEPTION`
    `ELECTROMAGNETIC FIELDS EXCLUSION`
    `INSTITUTE RADIOACTIVE CONTAMINATION, CHEMICAL, BIOLOGICAL, BIOCHEMICAL AND ELECTROMAGNETIC WEAPONS EXCLUSION CLAUSE`
    `PROFESSIONAL LIABILITY EXCLUSION`
    `SANCTION LIMITATION AND EXCLUSION CLAUSE`
    `SISTERSHIP EXCLUSION CLAUSE`
    `WAR AND TERRORISM EXCLUSION`

-- The answer on cover: a total enum, the absent outcome named with its reason.
DECLARE `The answer on cover` IS ONE OF
    `covered`
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `A reason there is no cover`

-- Condition 1 (src:185-190): what the audit of the earned premium leads to.
DECLARE `A premium adjustment` IS ONE OF
    `the Company returns the unearned portion` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the named insured pays the earned premium due` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `no adjustment`

-- Condition 5 (src:243-264): the basis on which the other insurance applies to the loss.
DECLARE `A basis of insurance` IS ONE OF
    `primary`
    `excess`
    `contingent`

-- Condition 5: one other policy that applies to the same loss.
DECLARE `Another insurance` HAS
    `applies to the loss on the basis of`              IS A `A basis of insurance`
    `the applicable limit of liability`                IS A NUMBER
    `provides for contribution by equal shares`        IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `A written notice of an occurrence`

-- Condition 3(a) (src:209-212) lists what the notice must contain. One field per item,
-- each a fact about the notice as given (writing-l4-rules phrasebook 6.2).
DECLARE `A written notice of an occurrence` HAS
    `in writing`                                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains particulars sufficient to identify the insured`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains reasonably obtainable information on the time, place and circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains the names and addresses of the injured`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains the names and addresses of available witnesses`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `given by or for the insured to the Company or one of its authorized agents`      IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Parties and acts, for the duties`

DECLARE `A party to the policy` IS ONE OF
    `the Company`
    `the named insured`
    `the insured`

DECLARE `An act under the policy` IS ONE OF
    `give written notice of the occurrence to the Company or an authorized agent`
    `forward every demand, notice, summons or other process received`
    `voluntarily make a payment, assume an obligation or incur an expense other than for first aid`
    `send copies of the premium records to the Company`
    `return the unearned portion of the premium`
    `withdraw, inspect, repair or replace the products or work, or take all reasonable steps to prevent further injury or damage`
    `execute and deliver instruments and papers to secure the rights of recovery`
    `do something after loss to prejudice the rights of recovery`
